# Phase 3 of the semantic-components design
# (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-21-semantic-presets-design.md, "The binding
# rule"). Structurally archeglyph has four element types; semantically people
# draw databases, queues, clients and third-party services. Those are all
# nodes. This is the rule that closes the gap.
#
# The rule lives here rather than beside the traversal in impl.ts because it
# is pure: given a tag, a theme's component names and that theme's default, it
# answers what the component should be, with no stylesheet and no diagram.
#
# VOCABULARY, fixed for both files in this pillar. A "component name" is the
# value of a style entry's `component` field. A "theme name" is a key of
# Stylesheet.themes. A component name may be qualified by a theme name
# ("acme.glyph"); unqualified means the theme name `default`. This file never
# says "binding" for either.

file: "packages/core/src/resolver/seed_bindings/derive.ts"
doc: "What component name an element should carry, given its `kind` tag."

methods: [
  { name: "deriveComponent"
    doc:
      "The component name an element should carry, or undefined for none.\n"
      "\n"
      "Three branches, tested in this order. The first is a guard that runs\n"
      "before `kind` is looked at at all:\n"
      "\n"
      "1. `themeDefault` undefined or empty -> undefined, whatever `kind` is.\n"
      "   A theme stating no default for this element type has no value that\n"
      "   means \"nobody chose\", so it opts out of the mechanism entirely.\n"
      "   deriveComponent(\"store\", [\"store\"], undefined) is undefined, NOT\n"
      "   \"store\".\n"
      "2. `componentNames` contains `kind` -> `kind`.\n"
      "3. otherwise -> `themeDefault`. An undefined or empty `kind` lands\n"
      "   here.\n"
      "\n"
      "Branch 2 compares `kind` to the entries of `componentNames` as exact\n"
      "raw strings. No qualifier is stripped from either side and none is\n"
      "added: a `kind` of \"default.store\" does not match a componentNames\n"
      "entry of \"store\" and falls to branch 3. A `kind` tag is diagram\n"
      "content, not a reference to a theme, so it never carries a theme name.\n"
      "\n"
      "Branch 3 is the common path and must not throw: the bundled themes\n"
      "ship no kind vocabulary on purpose, because design.md §4 makes themes\n"
      "shareable artifacts that cannot predict a consumer's tag scheme.\n"
      "deriveComponent(\"wormhole\", [\"glyph\"], \"glyph\") is \"glyph\".\n"
      "\n"
      "`componentNames` holds the names the theme defines for ONE element\n"
      "type; the caller chooses which list to pass. The returned string is\n"
      "always bare — this function never produces a qualified name."
    inputs: [
      { name: "kind", type: { unsupported: { reason: UNION_AT_TYPE_POSITION, source_excerpt: "string | undefined" } } },
      { name: "componentNames", type: { named: { symbol: "Array", args: [{ primitive: CHARACTER }] } } },
      { name: "themeDefault", type: { unsupported: { reason: UNION_AT_TYPE_POSITION, source_excerpt: "string | undefined" } } }
    ]
    output: { unsupported: { reason: UNION_AT_TYPE_POSITION, source_excerpt: "string | undefined" } }
  },
  { name: "isThemeDefault"
    doc:
      "Whether `current` is a component name meaning nobody chose it.\n"
      "\n"
      "True when `current` is undefined or the empty string.\n"
      "\n"
      "Otherwise both `current` and `themeDefault` are split by\n"
      "splitQualified into a theme name and a component name, with an\n"
      "unqualified string taking the theme name `default`. True when BOTH\n"
      "halves are equal; false when either differs.\n"
      "\n"
      "Splitting both sides is what makes the comparison survive a\n"
      "round-trip through something that writes qualified names. Worked\n"
      "cases, all with `themeDefault` = \"glyph\":\n"
      "  current = undefined        -> true\n"
      "  current = \"\"               -> true\n"
      "  current = \"glyph\"          -> true   (default/glyph vs default/glyph)\n"
      "  current = \"default.glyph\"  -> true   (default/glyph vs default/glyph)\n"
      "  current = \"acme.glyph\"     -> false  (theme name acme differs)\n"
      "  current = \"queue\"          -> false  (component name differs)\n"
      "\n"
      "\"acme.glyph\" being false is not an oversight: seeding acts only on\n"
      "the theme named `default`, so a component name pointing at any other\n"
      "theme was written deliberately and is left alone.\n"
      "\n"
      "`themeDefault` is never undefined or empty here. Its caller stops\n"
      "before calling this when the theme states no default for the element\n"
      "type, because deriveComponent has already returned undefined in that\n"
      "case and no component name is written at all."
    inputs: [
      { name: "current", type: { unsupported: { reason: UNION_AT_TYPE_POSITION, source_excerpt: "string | undefined" } } },
      { name: "themeDefault", type: { primitive: CHARACTER } }
    ]
    output: { primitive: BOOLEAN }
    uses: ["splitQualified"]
  }
]
